                                                       Milestones

A milestone is a marker attached to a task in a project that shows an important stage has been reached
This function can provide managers and other stakeholders with a high-level overview as to how a project is progressing.

Milestone path?
A milestone path is a ready-made list of milestones that projects can use.
That is the whole definition. A milestone is one marker. A milestone path is a list of markers.

Why we need milestone path
It is used ffor to mark improtant in project. to help track progress easilt 
A project has many tasks, and a manager or client needs to see progress without reading all of them. Milestones give a short list of the key stages.
Condition and progress status show whether the project is on schedule. They do not show which stage the project has reached. Milestones show the stage.
When every project uses the same milestones, as defined in a milestone path, projects can be compared and reported on together.

Where milestones are used in Workfront
A path is attached to the project. The project must be in Planning or Current status.
